      "writtenOn": "2026-04-27T15:08:51Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Talking offline, I\u0027m concerned about the need to track the texture views in the PassResourceUsageTracker, it\u0027s already very expensive and I\u0027d like to avoid adding more to it if possible.\n\nWhen we start using MTLHazardModeUntracked, we\u0027ll need a mechanism to keep resources alive until they are no longer needed. Let\u0027s introduce that alraedy, just for MTLTextureViews so that we don\u0027t need to call `useResource` on them.\n\nThe part of `useResource` that adds a memory barrier might be slightly pessimized by this because we don\u0027t tell Metal about subresource information. That seems ok, because looking at Metal4 there doesn\u0027t seem to be a way to tell to decompress framebuffer-compressed textures.",
      "revId": "ef939a297525d56e512604b0ecc6dfc8efaf272b",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
